1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,739
Two families of organic halogen compounds contain a benzene ring.

2
00:00:04,739 --> 00:00:12,200
In a haloarene, or aryl halide, the halogen sits directly on a ring carbon, like chlorobenzene.

3
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:17,187
In an aralkyl halide, like benzyl chloride, it sits on the side chain.

4
00:00:17,187 --> 00:00:20,065
The two behave completely differently.

